    "no_replacement_chars": true,
    "non_degenerate": true,
    "non_empty": true,
    "normalized_text": "The first note suggests that revenue should be recognized when the service is delivered, regardless of whether cash has been collected yet. This approach aligns with the principle of matching revenues and expenses to their respective periods.\n\nThe second note indicates that cash collection may happen later than expected and should not determine when revenue is recognized. This approach emphasizes recognizing revenue based on its economic reality rather than just timing in relation to cash collections.\n\nIn plain language:\n- **First Note**: Revenue happens as soon as services are provided.\n- **Second Note**: Revenue happens only after all payments for services have been received, even if it's later than initially anticipated.\n\nBoth notes",
